## 8. Observations (none blocking)

  O1  The pinned `why` is never asserted. All 29 entries carry a non-empty `why`
      (I checked), but containment.test.ts asserts only that each `disposition` is a
      recognized value; a future edit could blank a `why` and stay green. The `why`
      is the part a human reads when the census fires, so it is worth one line —
      `check("inventory B: every entry carries a why", PINNED_B.every(p => p.why.trim()))`.
      Not raised as a finding: the brief specifies the entry shape and the table, both
      of which are honoured, and no unasserted field is currently wrong.

  O2  The brief's own closing note is the right one to carry forward: "the proxy
      remains a proxy: the next miss will be a shape, not a spelling." Inventory B
      still cannot see a raw join built by string concatenation
      (`dir + "/" + id + ".md"`), by an array `.join()`, by `join(dir, id + ".md")`
      with no template at all, or by an id handed to a helper that appends the
      extension. These are declared limits, not defects — they are named in the brief
      and in the For-Sol section. Recorded here so the W-059 reviewer starts from the
      declared boundary rather than re-deriving it.

  O3  check advises `process.review_tier — review sella "qa-lead" ran on
      claude-fable-5, not an opus-tier model`. That is a finding about me, not about
      W-047. Noted so nobody reads it as a defect in the opus.

