## 10. Verdict

  PASS, round 2. All three round-1 findings are closed, and each was closed at the
  root rather than at the symptom:

    F-1  the spelling filter is deleted, not worked around; inventory B scans the
         shape the brief specifies; the pin widened from 12 to 29 with a disposition
         and a why for each; both spellings of acceptance check (e) now bite; mF's
         probe no longer reads as spelled to fit a scan; a ninth bypass the filter had
         been hiding (tick.ts:writeDailyActum) was surfaced, pinned `bypass`, and
         added to W-059's scope. My own independent re-derivation agrees with the pin
         entry for entry, in order, with nothing added or dropped.
    F-2  the refused-row assertion is falsifiable on all ten rows, proved by a mutant
         round 1's form could not have detected.
    F-3  mA/mB/mC carry disjoint, non-colliding, mutant-specific kills, and mA's
         recorded FAIL set demonstrably excludes mB's and mC's labels.
    F-4  the pattern is closed for this round: the deviation is authorized in the
         spec in advance, and disclosed in two commit messages and the traditio.

  The round-2 remedy also did the thing that most distinguishes a real fix from a
  patched symptom: widening the scan surfaced a bypass nobody had counted, and the
  builder reported it up rather than quietly pinning it — brief amendment 2 carries it
  into Intent, into the count, and into the follow-up opus.

  Everything I passed in round 1 still holds at 71dd3bb: four gates green, 33 mutants
  matching, the contract table's coverage, the collision-sentinel recipe at all nine
  rows, inventory A's alias- and reformat-proofing, and the harness's baseline,
  kills-AND and restore discipline.

  No conditions. W-047 is done as specified.
